# every text file is checked out exactly as it is stored, with LF, on every
# platform. git for windows checks text out with CRLF by default, and a file
# read with `include_str!` keeps those bytes where rustc normalises a literal's:
# `by_runner_columns.py` is `by`'s runner captured byte for byte, and its
# `_by_span` was cut out of it at "\n\n\ndef " and not found on any windows job
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd reads a batch file's labels by its CRLF line endings
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.jar binary
